

1) The Initial Visit:-
       You type localhost:3000/ and press Enter.
       The browser loads your React app.
       The Router wakes up, looks at the Address Bar (/), checks its <Routes> list, finds <Route path="/" element={<Landing />} />, and renders the Landing page.


2) useNavigate (The Instigator) =>(on clicking create board button)
       You click the button, which triggers Maps('/board/x7b9q2').


3) The Router (The Reactor)
        The moment the Address Bar changes, the Router hears an alarm go off.
        It immediately scans its list of <Routes>.
        It sees <Route path="/board/:roomId" element={<CanvasRoomWrapper />} />.
        It realizes the new URL matches this path. It instantly unmounts (destroys) the Landing Page and mounts (renders) the CanvasRoomWrapper component.

4) useParams (The Late Arrival)
        Now that the CanvasRoomWrapper is actively rendering on the screen, its code runs top-to-bottom.
        It hits const params = useParams();.
        useParams looks up at the current Address Bar, sees /board/x7b9q2, compares it to the Router's blueprint (/board/:roomId), and extracts the variable.
        It hands { roomId: 'x7b9q2' } to your component so you can pass it to your WebSocket server.